// Every URL below was fetched and its content checked against the organization
// it claims to be. Sites that block automated fetching (the Auditor's ISSG
// site, the Sheriff and the Xenia and Fairborn newspapers) were checked in a
// browser.
//
// THINGS THAT CHANGED SINCE JULY
//
//   * The Sheriff's Office and jail moved to 2295 Greene Way Blvd, Xenia
//     (December 2025); the Sheriff now has its own site.
//   * greenecountydod.org (Department of Development) has EXPIRED; the county's
//     own Department of Development page is used.
//   * The Family Violence Prevention Center is now Violence Free Futures.
//   * The Xenia Daily Gazette and Fairborn Daily Herald were bought by HD Media in
//     September 2026; both sites are current.
//   * The Auditor's property search is confirmed as ISSG.
//
// TRAPS
//
//   Greene County PA, NY, MO, TN, GA, VA, AL, NC, AR, IN, IA, MS; Beavercreek OR;
//   Jamestown NY/ND; Xenia IL. greenecountyohio.org is the visitors bureau, not
//   the county government.
//
// GEOGRAPHY
//
//   * Cities: Xenia (seat), Fairborn, Beavercreek and Bellbrook; Kettering,
//     Centerville, Huber Heights and Dayton reach in slightly and are left out.
//     Villages: Yellow Springs, Cedarville, Jamestown (with sites), Spring Valley,
//     Bowersville, Clifton. Xenia and Miami townships have sites.
//   * Seven school districts; Greene County ESC and Career Center; five
//     universities (Wright State, Central State, Wilberforce, Cedarville, Antioch).
//   * Wright-Patterson AFB and the National Museum of the U.S. Air Force straddle
//     Greene and Montgomery; the visitors bureau lists the museum.
//   * The Mental Health Recovery Board is shared with Clark and Madison
//     (Springfield). Fairborn Municipal Court also serves Beavercreek.
//
// LEFT OUT
//
//   * Caesar Creek State Park: Warren County.
//   * Beavercreek News-Current: no current stories found.
//   * Regional 9-1-1 center, land bank, port authority, humane society, community
//     foundation: no own websites found.

